Skills vendored from https://github.com/anthropics/skills
Commit 34040c9c568585f6929bedeaad110ad08f079624 (10 September 2026).

Every directory here is one skill from that repository's `skills/`
folder, copied byte for byte, and each carries its own LICENSE.txt: the
Apache License, Version 2.0, Copyright 2026 Anthropic, PBC. The
repository ships no NOTICE file of its own; THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md is
its third-party attribution file and is kept here unchanged (the fonts
under canvas-design/canvas-fonts are under the SIL Open Font License,
each with its OFL.txt beside it).

Not vendored, and why:

- docx, pdf, pptx, xlsx — their LICENSE.txt is not Apache: "Use of these
  materials ... is governed by your agreement with Anthropic". The
  desktop app already bundles them under that agreement.
- doc-coauthoring — carries no LICENSE.txt, no `license` frontmatter, and
  the repository has no top-level licence, so its terms are not
  established.

Modifications: none at rest. When a skill is served as an archive
(`polar/desktop/skill_store.py`) a `version` line is added to the
SKILL.md frontmatter so the desktop app can tell an installed copy from
a newer one; the catalogue's `version` is the upstream snapshot date.
